[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/comments/6254574165","html_url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/103274#issuecomment-6254574165","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/103274","id":6254574165,"node_id":"IC_kwDON91aY88AAAABdM06VQ","user":{"login":"bomtobe-hgkim","id":256723570,"node_id":"U_kgDOD01Kcg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256723570?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bomtobe-hgkim","html_url":"https://github.com/bomtobe-hgkim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bomtobe-hgkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bomtobe-hgkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bomtobe-hgkim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bomtobe-hgkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bomtobe-hgkim/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bomtobe-hgkim/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bomtobe-hgkim/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bomtobe-hgkim/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bomtobe-hgkim/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-18T20:09:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T20:09:53Z","body":"A regression test here could distinguish the cancellation request being accepted from the worker actually reaching a stopped state. For example, pause a child thread at a controllable tool boundary, issue stop, and assert that the UI stays at ‘stop requested’ until the worker exits; if it times out or emits another tool call, surface that as still running/stop failed rather than ‘stopped’. Also test a late completion racing with cancellation so it cannot overwrite the terminal state. I work on Orke at BOMTOBE, so I’m approaching this as an adjacent agent-workspace use case; I haven’t reproduced this report.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/comments/6254574165/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/comments/6354684609","html_url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/103274#issuecomment-6354684609","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/103274","id":6354684609,"node_id":"IC_kwDON91aY88AAAABesTKwQ","user":{"login":"samvallad33","id":143034159,"node_id":"U_kgDOCIaHLw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143034159?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/samvallad33","html_url":"https://github.com/samvallad33","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samvallad33/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samvallad33/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samvallad33/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samvallad33/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samvallad33/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samvallad33/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samvallad33/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samvallad33/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/samvallad33/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-23T00:49:25Z","updated_at":"2026-10-23T00:49:25Z","body":"Hi Tristyn,\n\nWhen you stopped the matching thread by hand, had it already changed any files in the manual match screens?\n\nWhat makes this worse than the wasted credits is that the coordinator reported one instruction to you and sent a different one to the thread, and you only caught it because you were watching closely. Your order was clear, ComicTagger first and matching on hold, yet the note that actually went out told that thread to keep building anyway. Once that gap exists, the coordinator is the only thing deciding what counts as paused, and its own summary is the only proof you get. A check living outside the agent, comparing what each thread was told and what it then did against the order you gave, would have flagged the mismatch before the credits went. The point from bomtobe-hgkim about separating stop requested from actually stopped fits right alongside that. Has it held off properly on threads since then?\n\nSam\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/comments/6354684609/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/comments/6355177726","html_url":"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/103274#issuecomment-6355177726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anthropics/claude-code/issues/103274","id":6355177726,"node_id":"IC_kwDON91aY88AAAABesxQ_g","user":{"login":"TRusselo","id":1154815,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNTQ4MTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1154815?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TRusselo","html_url":"https://github.com/TRusselo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TRusselo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TRusselo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TRusselo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TRusselo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TRusselo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TRusselo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TRusselo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TRuss